From a9e5f1d16ac55788e4d2becbb93d7f18026f8341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:36:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Merge manager and re-pin rulings, generalised into the
 skills and the watch loop

Writes the owner's rulings of 2026-11-06/07 into the skills that govern
them, each citing its ruling:

- remote-mount, index-config: a pin only moves forward ("Pin target", A);
  a re-pin is a cross-layer set; a re-pin that moves cat-harness-tools
  refreshes layer health ("Layer health", A; cat-harness-tools#1603).
- merge-manager-watcher: one merge manager; siblings send
  "ready: <repo>#<n> <sha>"; the owner approves there, one card per batch
  ("Approvals", B); P0-P3 order; every judge, shard tables included;
  approved non-workflow PRs get the merge-train label ("Train", A);
  workflow PRs merge directly ("Workflow PRs", A); runner relief
  ("Cancel CI").
- merge-queue: the sibling's side of the above, and the train ruling.
- continual-progress, coordinate: one pusher per PR branch; stacked PRs
  are retargeted, not merged into their base; the manager enforces pacing.
- merge-manager-watch.bpmn: runner relief before the meta-merge; an owner
  approval gate with a batch-card step; train or direct merge. SVG,
  checklist and .pot files regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
